Package: nginx-mod-brix-cache
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${brix:nginx-abi},
         curl,
         librados2,
         libradosstriper1,
         libvomsapi1t64 | libvomsapi1v5 | libvomsapi1
Provides: nginx-mod-xrootd (= ${binary:Version})
Description: BriX-Cache - XRootD, WebDAV, S3, CMS and metrics modules for nginx
 Dynamic nginx modules that serve files over the native XRootD stream
 protocol, WebDAV over HTTPS, and an S3-compatible HTTP subset, with CMS
 management-listener and Prometheus metrics support.
 .
 The modules must be built against the exact nginx version they are loaded
 into; this package's nginx dependency is therefore pinned to the version it
 was built for (see /usr/share/doc/nginx-mod-brix-cache/).
 .
 VOMS VO/FQAN ACL enforcement loads libvomsapi.so.1 at runtime via dlopen();
 curl(1) is fork/exec'd by legacy site scripts.  Both are declared explicitly
 because dpkg-shlibdeps cannot detect them from the ELF link records.

Package: brix-cache-client
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: brix-xrootdfs-fuse (= ${binary:Version}),
            brix-cvmfs-fuse (= ${binary:Version})
Provides: nginx-xrootd-client (= ${binary:Version})
Description: BriX-Cache clean-room native XRootD client tools (xrdcp, xrdfs, ...)
 Native command-line XRootD clients built clean-room on the in-tree protocol
 core (libbrix + libxrdproto) with NO libXrdCl / libXrdSec dependency:
 xrdcp, xrdfs, xrd, xrdcksum and checksum personalities, xrdqstats, xrdprep,
 xrdgsiproxy, xrddiag, xrdmapc, xrdgsitest, xrdstorascan, mpxstats-brix,
 xrdsssadmin-brix and wait41-brix, plus brix-fault-proxy (a root-free TCP
 fault-injection proxy for resilience testing) and the libbrixposix_preload.so
 LD_PRELOAD POSIX shim.  The FUSE mounts live in the brix-xrootdfs-fuse and
 brix-cvmfs-fuse packages (installed by default via Recommends).

Package: brix-cache-client-compat
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: brix-cache-client
Description: BriX-Cache native XRootD client tools under a brix- prefix
 The brix-cache-client tool set installed under a "brix-" prefix so it
 co-exists with the official xrootd-client package on one host: brix-xrdcp,
 brix-xrdfs, brix-xrd, brix-xrdcksum (and the checksum personalities
 brix-xrdadler32/brix-xrdcrc32c/brix-xrdcrc64), brix-xrdqstats, brix-wait41,
 brix-mpxstats, brix-xrdprep, brix-xrdgsiproxy, brix-xrddiag, brix-xrdmapc,
 brix-xrdgsitest, brix-xrdsssadmin and brix-xrdstorascan.  The binaries are
 byte-identical to brix-cache-client's; each self-identifies from argv[0], so
 usage/version/man output names the brix- alias, never the stock tool.  The
 Ceph operator tools ship prefixed in brix-tools-compat; the FUSE mounts are
 never prefixed and stay in brix-xrootdfs-fuse/brix-cvmfs-fuse.
 .
 The brix-env(7) manual page referenced by the tool man page footers ships in
 brix-cache-client (dpkg does not permit byte-identical shared ownership the
 way rpm does); install that package too if you want it.

Package: brix-xrootdfs-fuse
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fuse3
Description: BriX-Cache xrootdfs FUSE mount - root:// as a local filesystem
 The xrootdfs FUSE mount: presents a root:// (XRootD-protocol) endpoint as a
 local POSIX filesystem, built clean-room on the in-tree protocol core with no
 libXrdCl/libXrdSec dependency.  One binary carries both drivers - the async
 default and the synchronous --legacy engine.  Split out of brix-cache-client
 so a mount-only node (batch worker, interactive login host) can deploy and
 test it without the full CLI suite.
 .
 fuse3 is a hard dependency: xrootdfs forks/execs fusermount3 at
 mount/unmount time, which dpkg-shlibdeps cannot detect.

Package: brix-cvmfs-fuse
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fuse3
Recommends: cvmfs-config
Description: BriX-Cache brixMount FUSE client for cvmfs:// repositories
 brixMount: the native BriX CVMFS FUSE client.  Mounts cvmfs:// repositories
 (served by the BriX cvmfs:// site-cache protocol or stock stratum servers)
 with CAS verification and an optional writable overlay (cvmfs-rw), and also
 fronts the xrootdfs async driver via `brixMount xrootdfs <endpoint>`.  Split
 out of brix-cache-client so a cache/mount tier can deploy and test it
 standalone.
 .
 The cvmfs-config Recommends is a virtual package satisfied by
 brix-cvmfs-config or any stock cvmfs-config-* provider - repositories mount
 zero-config once a provider ships /etc/cvmfs keys and domain configuration.

Package: brix-cvmfs-automount
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, brix-cvmfs-fuse (= ${source:Version}), fuse3
Conflicts: cvmfs
Description: Automount /cvmfs via the brixMount autofs umbrella daemon
 Lazily mounts CVMFS repositories under /cvmfs on first access using the
 native `brixMount autofs` umbrella daemon (no autofs/systemd map dependency;
 children mount in a farm under /var/lib/brixcvmfs/.mnt and appear as
 symlinks).  Also ships the classic integration points - /usr/sbin/mount.cvmfs
 so `mount -t cvmfs` works, an /etc/auto.cvmfs program map for sites that
 prefer stock autofs, and a brixcvmfs@.service template for static per-repo
 mounts.  Enable with:
     systemctl enable --now brixcvmfs-automount
 .
 Conflicts with the stock cvmfs package: both own /usr/sbin/mount.cvmfs,
 /etc/auto.cvmfs and the same /cvmfs automount role.

Package: brix-cvmfs-config
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Provides: cvmfs-config (= ${source:Version})
Conflicts: cvmfs-config-default, cvmfs-config-egi, cvmfs-config-osg
Description: Default CVMFS configuration and master keys for CVMFS-brix
 Default domain configuration (cern.ch, egi.eu, opensciencegrid.org stratum-1
 sets) and the upstream-published master public keys, vendored byte-identical
 from the stock cvmfs-config-default package (provenance and fingerprints in
 /etc/cvmfs/keys/README.md).  Everything under /etc is a dpkg conffile:
 operator edits and rotated keys survive upgrades.

Package: brix-cache-tests
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         nginx-mod-brix-cache (= ${source:Version}),
         brix-cache-client (= ${source:Version}),
         nginx,
         python3,
         python3-pytest,
         python3-pytest-timeout,
         python3-pytest-xdist,
         python3-cryptography,
         python3-requests,
         python3-urllib3
Suggests: python3-xrootd
Description: Integration and conformance test-suite for BriX-Cache
 The full pytest integration, conformance, and adversarial test-suite for
 BriX-Cache (root://, WebDAV, S3, CMS, metrics, FRM, TPC, ...), installed
 under /usr/share/brix.  Run with, e.g.:
     cd /usr/share/brix && PYTHONPATH=tests python3 -m pytest tests/ -v
 .
 python3-xrootd (the official XRootD python bindings) is only needed by the
 cross-backend / reference-daemon comparison tests and is not packaged in the
 Ubuntu archive, hence Suggests.

Package: brix-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         librados2,
         libradosstriper1,
         libcephfs2
Recommends: python3-rados, python3-cephfs
Provides: brix-cache-ceph-tools (= ${binary:Version})
Description: XrdCeph/CephFS migration and rescue operator tools for BriX-Cache
 XrdCeph <-> CephFS migration tools with zero-move redirect mode,
 rollback/finalize support, and site-profile configuration: compiled C++
 primaries (xrdceph_striper_migrate, xrdceph_cephfs_to_striper) plus the
 pure-Python variants (*.py, libexec-backed pymigrate package) with JSONL
 output and resumable state, and the offline rescue utilities
 xrdrados_rescue, xrdcephfs_rescue, and xrdceph_migrate.
 .
 The .py tool variants import the distro rados/cephfs python bindings at run
 time (Recommends); the compiled tools need neither.

Package: brix-tools-compat
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         librados2,
         libradosstriper1,
         libcephfs2
Description: BriX-Cache XrdCeph/CephFS operator tools under a brix- prefix
 The compiled brix-tools Ceph/CephFS migration + rescue operators installed
 under a "brix-" prefix so they co-install with any stock-named counterparts:
 brix-xrdceph_striper_migrate, brix-xrdceph_cephfs_to_striper,
 brix-xrdrados_rescue, brix-xrdcephfs_rescue and brix-xrdceph_migrate.  Each
 self-identifies from argv[0].  The pure-Python migration variants are not
 prefixed and remain in brix-tools.
